PATCH 557: the last two SETTLED constant-false sentinels.

Same class as patches 548 and 551 -- a `uint16_t` promotes to `int`, so a Ghidra-emitted `== -1` can
never be true and the guard is dead.  board:0022 carries the class; these are the two remaining members
whose width and constant are both proven from the image.

## DGROUP:0xe82e -- `DAT_2000_a82e`

Nine references, every one word-width, and the one the port renders as `== -1` is unambiguous:

    cb74: c7 06 2e e8 ff ff   movw  $0xffff,0xe82e
    cb7c: c7 06 2e e8 00 00   movw  $0x0,0xe82e
    cbd8: c7 06 2e e8 02 00   movw  $0x2,0xe82e
    cf8e: 83 3e 2e e8 02      cmpw  $0x2,0xe82e
    cfe2: 83 3e 2e e8 02      cmpw  $0x2,0xe82e
    d176: 83 3e 2e e8 02      cmpw  $0x2,0xe82e
    d199: 83 3e 2e e8 ff      cmpw  $0xffff,0xe82e     <- the site
    d1b0: 83 3e 2e e8 00      cmpw  $0x0,0xe82e
   1b676: 83 3e 2e e8 02      cmpw  $0x2,0xe82e

## DGROUP:0x18e4 -- `DAT_1000_d8e4`, the ready-queue head

`DAT_1000_XXXX` with XXXX >= 0xc000 is DGROUP XXXX-0xc000 (see patch 553), so this is DGROUP:0x18e4 --
the queue head the port's own patch-comment for `FUN_1000_3907` already calls `[0x18e4]`:

   13455: c7 06 e4 18 ff ff   movw  $0xffff,0x18e4
   135b8: 83 3e e4 18 ff      cmpw  $0xffff,0x18e4
   135e7: 8b 1e e4 18         mov   0x18e4,%bx
   135ec: a3 e4 18            mov   %ax,0x18e4
   13915: 83 3e e4 18 ff      cmpw  $0xffff,0x18e4     <- the site, inside FUN_1000_3907 (asm 0x13907)

This one is not cosmetic.  `FUN_1000_3907` returns the carry that `FUN_0000_e714`'s idle loop branches
on -- patch's own note: "stc/lret when [0x3e00]!=0 or the queue is EMPTY [0x18e4]==0xffff", and `jae`
in e714 means CF=1 runs the idle housekeeping.  With `!= -1` always true, the port cleared CF whenever
`[0x3e00]` was zero, i.e. it reported "event queue non-empty" even when the queue was empty, and the
idle path never ran on that condition.

## Still not settled, and deliberately left

`DAT_1000_e02e` (DGROUP:0x202e) has NO plausible absolute-displacement reference in the image, so its
width cannot be read the way the others were -- it is reached through a base register or is a
register-modelled temporary.  It also carries the `< 0` subclass (`DAT_1000_e02e < 0` on an unsigned is
equally a constant false) and sits in a 32-bit compare helper Ghidra otherwise treats as signed
(SBORROW2, and a `(int)` cast on one of its two `< 0` tests but not the other).  Width and signedness
have to be settled together there, from the containing function, not from a displacement scan.

board:0022

--- a/fist.c
+++ b/fist.c
@@ -35466,7 +35466,7 @@
 void __allregs FUN_0000_d199(void)
 
 {
-  if (DAT_2000_a82e == -1) {
+  if (DAT_2000_a82e == 0xffff) {  /* PATCH 557: d199 cmpw $0xffff,0xe82e */
     DAT_2000_a85d = 4;
     DAT_2000_a8ee = 3;
     DAT_2000_a8f8 = 3;
@@ -50071,7 +50071,7 @@
   /* PATCH: restore the dropped CF return (asm 0x13907: clc/lret when the event queue is non-empty,
    * stc/lret when [0x3e00]!=0 or the queue is empty [0x18e4]==0xffff).  Ghidra dropped the flag ops.
    * CF drives the caller's `jae` (e714 idle loop: CF=1 => run idle housekeeping c52c/096c). */
-  if ((DAT_1000_fe00 == '\0') && (DAT_1000_d8e4 != -1)) {
+  if ((DAT_1000_fe00 == '\0') && (DAT_1000_d8e4 != 0xffff)) {  /* PATCH 557: 13915 cmpw $0xffff,0x18e4 */
     g_fist_cf = 0;   /* 1391c clc; lret (queue non-empty) */
     return;
   }
